WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.828
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.128 --> 00:00:08.723
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:16.064
Unit twenty-three: Saving the Planet at Home. Today you will suggest eco-friendly actions with can and could.

4
00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:19.190
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.529
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.408
Recycle.

7
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.786
Recycle means to process used things so they can be used again.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.499
We recycle bottles and cans.

9
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:36.119
Your turn. Say: Recycle.

10
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:39.991
Recycle.

11
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.670
Reuse.

12
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.578
Reuse means to use something again.

13
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:47.253
I reuse my shopping bags.

14
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.073
Your turn. Say: Reuse.

15
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:53.923
Reuse.

16
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:55.777
Reduce.

17
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:59.503
Reduce means to make something smaller or less.

18
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:01.977
We can reduce plastic at home.

19
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:05.294
Your turn. Say: Reduce.

20
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.123
Reduce.

21
00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:11.024
Electricity.

22
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:15.084
Electricity means power for lights and machines.

23
00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:17.950
Turn off the lights to save electricity.

24
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.400
Your turn. Say: Electricity.

25
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:25.409
Electricity.

26
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.105
Water.

27
00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:30.290
Water means the clear liquid we drink.

28
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.127
Don't waste water when you brush your teeth.

29
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:35.847
Your turn. Say: Water.

30
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.539
Water.

31
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:41.261
Plastic.

32
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.515
Plastic means a light material that lasts a very long time.

33
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:48.418
Plastic bags pollute the rivers.

34
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.820
Your turn. Say: Plastic.

35
00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:55.586
Plastic.

36
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.386
Compost.

37
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:01.323
Compost means to turn food waste into soil.

38
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.265
We compost fruit peels in the garden.

39
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.595
Your turn. Say: Compost.

40
00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:11.400
Compost.

41
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:12.930
Habit.

42
00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:16.392
Habit means something you do regularly.

43
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:19.006
Saving water is a good habit.

44
00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:22.141
Your turn. Say: Habit.

45
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.769
Habit.

46
00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:30.171
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:34.003
Visal, what eco-friendly habits does your family have?

48
00:02:35.117 --> 00:02:37.163
We reuse our bags at the market.

49
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.264
Great! What else could you do?

50
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.545
We could compost our food waste in the garden.

51
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.023
And electricity?

52
00:02:48.117 --> 00:02:52.650
We can turn off the fan when we leave the room. Small habits matter!

53
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.207
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.758
Grammar focus: Can and could for suggestions.

55
00:02:59.058 --> 00:03:00.268
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:02.414
We could reuse bags.

57
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:04.898
We can recycle bottles.

58
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:07.574
You could take shorter showers.

59
00:03:08.533 --> 00:03:13.554
'Can' says it is possible. 'Could' sounds softer and more polite when you suggest an idea.

60
00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:17.631
Be careful! Don't say: We could reusing bags.

61
00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.984
Say: We could reuse bags.

62
00:03:22.284 --> 00:03:24.876
After can or could, use the base verb.

63
00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:28.226
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.905
Small Habits, Big Change.

65
00:03:31.205 --> 00:03:32.798
We can save the planet at home.

66
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.100
We can reduce plastic, reuse bags and recycle bottles.

67
00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.622
We could turn off the electricity we don't need.

68
00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:44.202
We could save water and compost food waste.

69
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.850
Small habits matter when every family does them.

70
00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:52.819
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:53.683 --> 00:03:56.777
We blank reuse our bags. It's a good idea.

72
00:03:57.077 --> 00:04:00.045
A, could. B, couldn't. C, mustn't.

73
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.228
The answer is A: could.

74
00:04:06.383 --> 00:04:08.255
To use something again is to blank.

75
00:04:08.555 --> 00:04:11.988
A, reuse. B, reduce. C, compost.

76
00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:17.649
The answer is A: reuse.

77
00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:21.398
To turn food waste into soil is to blank.

78
00:04:21.698 --> 00:04:25.642
A, compost. B, recycle. C, plastic.

79
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.049
The answer is A: compost.

80
00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:35.524
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:39.184
What is one eco-friendly habit your family has?

82
00:04:47.983 --> 00:04:49.484
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:49.784 --> 00:04:58.345
My family reuses glass bottles for water. We could also compost our food waste, so I asked my mother to start next week.

84
00:04:58.645 --> 00:05:00.390
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:01.283 --> 00:05:05.608
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and can and could for suggestions.

86
00:05:05.908 --> 00:05:12.647
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

87
00:05:12.947 --> 00:05:15.843
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

88
00:05:16.143 --> 00:05:19.259
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

